purpose: The only module that knows what a window is. SDL lives here and nowhere else.

allow: util gfx media

public: InputEvent.h SdlWindow.h SdlPresenter.h SdlAudioDevice.h Sandbox.h AppDirectories.h SystemFonts.h DescriptorWait.h

extern: SDL3

max_tu_lines: 800

# The fifteenth method is the wait that also watches sockets -- ADR 0011. It is
# here rather than in app because this module is where the process is allowed
# to sleep, and that rule is what lets the loop policy be tested with no window
# system present.
# The fourth member is the physical key of a press SDL is still describing.
# ADR 0017 §1 splits a key event into what key it was, what it means and what it
# inserts; SDL splits the same press into two events, one carrying each half, so
# something has to hold one until the other arrives. It belongs to the window
# because the event queue does.
budget: SdlWindow      header_lines=105 public_methods=15 members=4
# A key event, which is now five facts and not four: what character it made,
# what named key it was, which physical key that is, what was held, and whether
# the platform's auto-repeat produced it. The physical key is the one that
# cannot be recovered downstream -- 'a' is KeyA on QWERTY and KeyQ on AZERTY --
# which is why it is on this side of the seam. ADR 0017 §1.
budget: KeyEvent      header_lines=30 public_methods=0 members=6
budget: SdlPresenter   header_lines=60 public_methods=6  members=3
budget: AppDirectories header_lines=50 public_methods=6  members=3
# Owns a catalog, an index of what is installed, and the fallback family. The
# index is the reason this is not just a gfx::FontCatalog: it holds paths, not
# faces, so a desktop's worth of fonts costs a list of strings rather than
# hundreds of megabytes.
# 75 lines and a thirteenth method for ADR 0024's RegisterWebFont: the provider
# every real binary uses had inherited the base class's honest refusal, so a page's
# `@font-face` registered in the tests and nowhere else.
# ADR 0028 §4's device. Small because the callback is small on purpose: it drains the ring
# and does nothing else -- no allocation, no lock, no document -- and the header says why
# each of those is a rule rather than a preference.
budget: SdlAudioDevice   header_lines=55 public_methods=10 members=4
# +1 member and +15 lines for per-character font fallback: the coverage cache, keyed by
# 256-code-point block. Without it a page of Japanese probes every installed face once per
# character; with it, once per script.
# +1 member and +17 lines for the resolution cache. FontFor is three full passes
# -- every font file on the machine, every loaded face, then the catalog's own
# match -- to answer a question about the *request*, and layout asks it for the
# width, the line height and the ascent of every text run. It is dropped when a
# face is loaded, which is the only event that can change an answer.
budget: SystemFontProvider header_lines=115 public_methods=14 members=5
